---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
import MediaFigure from '../../components/MediaFigure.astro';
import { ASSETS } from '../../data/assets';
import { SKILLS } from '../../data/mastery';

const title = 'Resonance: A Plague Tale Legacy Skills & Combat Guide';
const description =
  'Resonance skills: Sophia’s six skills and their masteries, what each one does, the 165 Resonance Point cost, and which to buy first.';
const crumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'Skills', url: '/skills/' },
];
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} pageType="collection" breadcrumbs={crumbs}>
  <div class="container py-10">
    <Breadcrumb items={crumbs} />
    <header class="mt-6 max-w-3xl">
      <p class="section-kicker">Skills &amp; combat</p>
      <h1 class="section-title">Resonance: A Plague Tale Legacy combat and skills</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-lg text-fog">
        Sophia has six skills, each with two masteries, plus a Focus Attack she gets from the story.
        Unlocking everything costs 165 of the 200 Resonance Points in the game.
      </p>
    </header>
    <div class="mt-8"><MediaFigure {...ASSETS.spherePuzzle} /></div>

    <section class="prose-page mt-10 max-w-3xl">
      <h2>How skills work</h2>
      <p>
        Skills are bought with Resonance Points, 200 of which are spread across the chapters.
        The Steam achievement <strong>Like a warrior</strong> ("Unlock the 6 mastery branches")
        confirms the six-branch structure. Each new skill branch costs more than the last, so the
        order you buy in decides how much of the game you spend under-equipped.
      </p>
      <p>
        The margin is 35 points, and it is smaller than it looks: Resonance Points only save when you
        reach the next checkpoint, they do not carry through Story Select, and you cannot farm them on
        a replay. Sweep dead ends on your first pass. The
        <a href="/plague-tale-legacy-collectibles-by-chapter/">collectibles by chapter guide</a> has
        the full rules.
      </p>
      <p>
        Focus Attack is free. It unlocks through the story, fills as you attack, parry, and dodge, and
        sweeps everything around Sophia when it is full.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 max-w-3xl">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-bone">The six skills</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fog">
        Listed in the unlock order walkthrough notes recommend. Details and the reasoning are in the
        <a href="/plague-tale-legacy-skills-unlock-order/" class="text-wheat underline">skills unlock order guide</a>.
      </p>
      <ol class="mt-6 space-y-5">
        {
          SKILLS.map((skill, i) => (
            <li class="surface p-5">
              <h3 class="text-xl font-black text-bone">
                {i + 1}. {skill.name}
              </h3>
              <p class="mt-2 text-fog">{skill.effect}</p>
              <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fog">
                <strong class="text-bone">Masteries:</strong> {skill.masteries}
              </p>
              <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fog">
                <strong class="text-bone">When to buy:</strong> {skill.when}
              </p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="prose-page mt-10 max-w-3xl">
      <h2>When to change the order</h2>
      <p>
        The order is a default. If red attacks are ending your attempts, finish Aegean Deflect before
        anything else. If you keep getting hit from the side in crowded rooms, move Bullbreaker Kick or
        Echo's Return up. If dodging is the problem, take Hero's Step earlier.
      </p>

      <h2>More combat guides</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/combat/">Combat and parry guide</a> — parrying, flanking guards, and the attack colour cues.</li>
        <li><a href="/stealth-or-combat/">Stealth or combat</a> — when to sneak, when to fight, and dark rooms.</li>
        <li><a href="/plague-tale-legacy-all-bosses/">All bosses</a> — Cadmos, Cercyon, Faro, Irene, King Minos, and Asterion.</li>
        <li><a href="/minoan-sphere-light-puzzle-guide/">Minoan sphere and light puzzles</a> — the sphere's powers and the chapter puzzles.</li>
        <li><a href="/weapons/">Weapons</a> — the eight Blades and where to find them.</li>
        <li><a href="/resonance-inherited-brutality-adaptable/">Inherited brutality and Adaptable</a> — the rare combat achievements.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
